  "answer": "Two small bugs, exactly as described:\n\n- `src/config.ts` — `Boolean(value)` treats `'false'` and `1` as enabled; must accept only the literal `true`.\n- `src/display.ts` — both ternary branches return `'ON'`; the false branch must return `'OFF'`.\n\nFixing both while preserving the exported APIs:\nNow verifying with the existing test suite:\nBoth repairs are in place and verified:\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/config.ts` — `enabled(value)` now returns `value === true`, so only the literal `true` enables the feature (no more truthy coercion of `'false'`, `1`, etc.).\n- `src/display.ts` — `display(value)` now returns `'OFF'` in the false branch instead of the duplicated `'ON'`.\n\n**Verification**\n```\nbun test v1.3.14\n(pass) strict feature state reaches display\n 1 pass · 0 fail · 6 expect() calls\n```\n\nThe existing test confirms all non-`true` inputs (`false`, `'false'`, `1`, `null`, `undefined`) render `OFF`, while `true` renders `ON`. Both exported APIs (`enabled`, `display`) and the test file are unchanged."
